{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TjsRfmJ9LPRjCUhPY4a3Wz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, here is the answer:\\\\n\\\\n## DSL Opt-in Support Property Name Change\\\\n\\\\nIn **KIP-1285: DSL Opt-in Support for Header-Aware State Stores**, the StreamsConfig property name was changed from **`dsl.store.type`** to **`dsl.store.format`** in response to reviewer feedback.\\\\n\\\\n### Reviewer Feedback\\\\n\\\\n**Lucas Brutschy** raised the concern in the KIP-1285 discussion thread (in `/store/kips/KIP-1285/2026-02-23-discuss-KIP-1285-DSL-header-aware-state-stores-a75c98ed.md`):\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"The config name `dsl.store.type` feels a bit ambiguous since we already have `dsl.store.suppliers.class` (which controls RocksDB vs. in-memory). `dsl.store.type` could be confused with that distinction. Would something like `dsl.store.format` be clearer, since this is really about the value format (timestamped vs. timestamped+headers)?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Matthias J. Sax** agreed with this feedback, stating \\\\\\\"I like Lucas' idea about 'format' vs 'type'.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n### KIP Author's Response\\\\n\\\\n**Alieh Saeedi** (the KIP author) responded positively: \\\\\\\"dsl.store.type makes sense to me, but I'm not attached to it. I can change it (and already have changed it) to dsl.store.format if we prefer that naming.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe enum was also renamed from `DslStoreType` to **`DslStoreFormat`** with values `DEFAULT` and `HEADERS`.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1285/2026-02-23-discuss-KIP-1285-DSL-header-aware-state-stores-a75c98ed.md`\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1285/2026-02-23-discuss-KIP-1285-DSL-header-aware-state-stores-2378b0e1.md`\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"kips/KIP-1285/2026-02-23-discuss-KIP-1285-DSL-header-aware-state-stores-2378b0e1.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1285/2026-02-23-discuss-KIP-1285-DSL-header-aware-state-stores-a75c98ed.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":28.21,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":110606,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":20129,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0625416,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":2233}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92761401-fda0-4b6a-8c1b-0d9580da1b68","uuid":"f9262268-3eb3-4879-93cc-6d42332f5011","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:54:40.503Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, here is the answer:\\\\n\\\\n## DSL Opt-in Support Property Name Change\\\\n\\\\nIn **KIP-1285: DSL Opt-in Support for Header-Aware State Stores**, the StreamsConfig property name was changed from **`dsl.store.type`** to **`dsl.store.format`** in response to reviewer feedback.\\\\n\\\\n### Reviewer Feedback\\\\n\\\\n**Lucas Brutschy** raised the concern in the KIP-1285 discussion thread (in `/store/kips/KIP-1285/2026-02-23-discuss-KIP-1285-DSL-header-aware-state-stores-a75c98ed.md`):\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"The config name `dsl.store.type` feels a bit ambiguous since we already have `dsl.store.suppliers.class` (which controls RocksDB vs. in-memory). `dsl.store.type` could be confused with that distinction. Would something like `dsl.store.format` be clearer, since this is really about the value format (timestamped vs. timestamped+headers)?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Matthias J. Sax** agreed with this feedback, stating \\\\\\\"I like Lucas' idea about 'format' vs 'type'.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n### KIP Author's Response\\\\n\\\\n**Alieh Saeedi** (the KIP author) responded positively: \\\\\\\"dsl.store.type makes sense to me, but I'm not attached to it. I can change it (and already have changed it) to dsl.store.format if we prefer that naming.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe enum was also renamed from `DslStoreType` to **`DslStoreFormat`** with values `DEFAULT` and `HEADERS`.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1285/2026-02-23-discuss-KIP-1285-DSL-header-aware-state-stor